{"name":"Spring Lawn","hex":"#cbdd94","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spring","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move or burst forth.","To appear."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of springing: a leap, a jump.","The season of the year in temperate regions in which temperatures and daylight hours rise, and plants spring from the ground and into bloom and dormant animals spring to life."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spring"},{"term":"lawn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ground (generally in front of or around a house) covered with grass kept closely mown.","An open space between woods."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To furnish with a lawn."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lawn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spring Lawn","blocks":[{"text":"Spring Lawn is an historic home on Kemble Street in Lenox, Massachusetts. Built in 1904 for John Alexandre, the mansion is considered a unique blend of Beaux-Arts and Classical Revival styles. Spring Lawn was designed by Guy Lowell who was also the architect of the Museum of Fine Arts, Boston and the New York Supreme Court courthouse. The property has seen many uses over the years, including acting as the home of the National Music Foundation, Carl H. Stevens Jr.'s Bible Speaks College, and Shakespeare & Company. Today, there are plans to convert the mansion and its surrounding property into a luxury resort."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_Lawn"},{"title":"Lawn","blocks":[{"text":"A lawn is an area of soil-covered land planted with grasses and other durable plants such as clover which is maintained at a short height with a lawn mower and used for aesthetic and recreational purposes. It is also commonly referred to as part of a garden."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/The_Lawn_UVa_2007.jpg/330px-The_Lawn_UVa_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawn"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/L%C3%B6tstugan_B%C3%A4rbo_Nyk%C3%B6pings_kommun.jpg/500px-L%C3%B6tstugan_B%C3%A4rbo_Nyk%C3%B6pings_kommun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/L%C3%B6tstugan_B%C3%A4rbo_Nyk%C3%B6pings_kommun.jpg/1280px-L%C3%B6tstugan_B%C3%A4rbo_Nyk%C3%B6pings_kommun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/L%C3%B6tstugan_B%C3%A4rbo_Nyk%C3%B6pings_kommun.jpg/500px-L%C3%B6tstugan_B%C3%A4rbo_Nyk%C3%B6pings_kommun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The lawn of a small summerhouse","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AL%C3%B6tstugan_B%C3%A4rbo_Nyk%C3%B6pings_kommun.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Croquetplayers.jpg/500px-Croquetplayers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Croquetplayers.jpg/1280px-Croquetplayers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Croquetplayers.jpg/500px-Croquetplayers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A croquet lawn at a club in Edinburgh, Scotland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACroquetplayers.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/San_Francisco_Botanical_Garden_Great_Lawn_1.jpg/500px-San_Francisco_Botanical_Garden_Great_Lawn_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/San_Francisco_Botanical_Garden_Great_Lawn_1.jpg/1280px-San_Francisco_Botanical_Garden_Great_Lawn_1.jpg?utm